    m_MinSize: 1
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'Note: Asset Bundle loading has been removed with the addressables update.
    Asset Bundles should now be managed by the addressables system. This scene has
    been kept because it is a popular scene to base character creators on. However,
    the asset bundle downloading will no longer work.



    Click on a character
    and then click the ''Get Extra Content'' UI button to see the demo asset bundles
    content you can load (located in the project in ''UMA/ Examples/ DynamicCharacterSystem
    Examples/ Assets/ DemoAssetBundles'')


    On a fresh install of UMA these assets
    will be loaded directly from the project using AssetBundles ''Simulation Mode''.
    This is actually much slower than actual asset bundles!


    To test *actual*
    asset bundles, go to ''UMA/ AssetBundleManager Settings'' in  the main menu.
    In there click ''Build AssetBundles'', enable the testing server and play again.


    Built
    assetBundles are stored outside the ''Assets'' folder in ''AssetBundles/[Platform]''
    and the testing server loads them from here.


    To test remote assetBundles,
    you can upload the ''AssetBundles/[Platform]'' folder to a server and put a link
    to the containing assetbundles folder into the ''Remote Server URL'' field in
    the DynamicAssetLoader object in the scene.


    Because UMAAssetBundleManager
    handles loading of the correct assetbundles for the current platform, you only
    need to ensure your built bundles are uploaded inside the generated platform
    folder. The URL you assign to DynamicAssetLoader should NOT contain any platform
    name (eg it should just be ''https://mygreatserver/assetbundles/'' NOT ''https://mygreatserver/assetbundles/[Platform]'')

'
